 "quest_dossier": "# Quests of Sergeant Cargug (Briarwood)\n\n# Sergeant Cargug (npc 9500000209, name_string 10297): unbuilt quest dossier\n\n**Scope.** Four unbuilt quests are cited for Cargug. Ids are the `ucdt` keys from `refs:opening-anvil-placement-v1/locale/en_us_data.dat` (line numbers given). The `locale` tool did not accept these keys (\"no such id\"), so text was copied from that file. Its own numeric ids (e.g. 9832) are a different index. Nothing below is a reward, level or prerequisite unless marked. Quest titles were not found in the client for A, B or D.\n\n**Already built, skipped:** Chapter 1: The Weapon Shipment (E9, title ucdt 2603070786, in `quests/adventurer.json` ~line 2951). Chapter 1: It's Business Time (E13, title ucdt 1908825225, built ~line 3163). Its intro is Amaranthus, 575707451, which is Cargug's line. The taste-tester escort (275365818) is a step in the Nomnomalug/Darkthorne chain. It is already covered in `npcs/wugachug.json` ~line 11243, and Cargug only relays \"safe passage\" there, so it is not listed as his quest.\n\n---\n\n## A. Treeleaf's Retreat (Cargug's Treeleaf quest)\n\n- **Title:** no client title string found. The name \"Treeleaf's Retreat\" comes from the record only. (R)\n- **Intro (offer):** `3309875870` \"Cargug has asked you to defeat Treeleaf, a creature that is imposing its will on the Hedge Maze.<BR><BR>Enter Treeleaf's Retreat and put a stop to him!\" (en_us_data.dat:87493). Evidence: `notes/Build Guides/Content/Dungeons/Treeleaf's Retreat.md` lines 85-87.\n- **Companion offer line:** `3158050844` \"There is a rather large and nasty-tempered tree-fellow that has set up residence within the Hedge Maze in an area called Treeleaf's Retreat. His name is... you guessed it! Treeleaf! I want you to defeat him before he can take over more of the maze! How 'bout it?\"",
